+# Permanent-liquidity scan with Nuthatch (opt-in)
+
+Issue #2048 replays every Transfer of a fungible LP token from genesis through `eth_getLogs`. This
+script is an optional way to do that replay locally with [Nuthatch](https://github.com/nuthatch-org/nuthatch),
+a single-binary indexer. Nothing in the Worker, D1, the DEX registry or scoring uses it.
+
+## Run it
+
+```
+npm run scan:permanent-liquidity -- --rpc <archive eth_getLogs URL> --dir ~/lp-scan \
+  0xLpToken:firstBlock [0xOtherLp:firstBlock ...]
+```
+
+It writes a nest (one ERC-20 Transfer ABI, one contract entry per token) into `--dir`, runs
+`nuthatch dev --seal-direct` until the history is sealed, rebuilds balances, and checks
+`replay(non-zero holders) + balanceOf(0x0) == totalSupply()` at the tip. A token that fails the check
+is a failed scan. Re-running in the same `--dir` resumes; it never starts over.
+
+Needs Node 20+, the `nuthatch` binary on PATH (or `--nuthatch <path>`) and an archive RPC.
+
+## Measured
+
+Two LP tokens from block 10,000,000 to 26,450,931, one public RPC (Tenderly gateway), 4 parallel
+windows of 5,000 blocks, one laptop: 7m26s, 109,446 Transfer events, both supply checks pass.
